proposed_comments.body:
### Stop page-level dispatch after a visible selection chord

**Severity:** `high`

Returning `false` for a visible Alt+Shift+digit target lets `ShellPage_OnPreviewKeyDown` continue into command-keybinding dispatch. If the focused shelf item has an action bound to the same chord, that action can execute instead of the shortcut only moving focus. Stop this page-level path while leaving `e.Handled` unchanged so WinUI can still invoke the native access key.

```suggestion
        switch (QuickAccessShelfShortcuts.ResolveSelectionShortcut(
            e.Key,
            modifiers.Ctrl,
            modifiers.Alt,
            modifiers.Shift,
            modifiers.Win,
            QuickAccessShelf.VisibleItemCount,
            isKeyTipDisplayMode: AccessKeyManager.IsDisplayModeEnabled))
        {
            case QuickAccessShelfShortcuts.SelectionShortcutTarget.Visible:
                // Let the matching native access key move focus to the requested shelf item.
                return true;
            case QuickAccessShelfShortcuts.SelectionShortcutTarget.Unavailable:
                // Reserve shelf selection chords even when their targets are in overflow so
                // they cannot invoke a context shortcut on the currently focused shelf item.
                e.Handled = true;
                return true;
        }
```

Apply this together with the shortcut-helper update below.

### Recognize the shortcut while key-tip mode is active

**Severity:** `medium`

WinUI can keep access-key display mode active after Alt has been released, in which case the subsequent shifted digit arrives with `alt == false`. Requiring the modifier bit unconditionally makes the advertised selection shortcut fail for that normal key-tip sequence. Accepting active key-tip mode preserves both press orders while retaining the Ctrl, Shift, Win, and digit checks.

```suggestion
    public static bool IsSelectionShortcut(VirtualKey key, bool ctrl, bool alt, bool shift, bool win, bool isKeyTipDisplayMode = false) =>
        (alt || isKeyTipDisplayMode) &&
        IsSelectionAccessKey(ctrl, shift, win) &&
        GetTopRowShortcutIndex(key) >= 0;

    public static SelectionShortcutTarget ResolveSelectionShortcut(
        VirtualKey key,
        bool ctrl,
        bool alt,
        bool shift,
        bool win,
        int visibleItemCount,
        bool isKeyTipDisplayMode = false)
    {
        if (!IsSelectionShortcut(key, ctrl, alt, shift, win, isKeyTipDisplayMode))
        {
            return SelectionShortcutTarget.None;
        }

        return GetTopRowShortcutIndex(key) < visibleItemCount
            ? SelectionShortcutTarget.Visible
            : SelectionShortcutTarget.Unavailable;
    }
```

Please also add focused coverage for the released-Alt/key-tip-mode path.
